On Mon, Jul 23, 2001 at 09:15:01AM -0400, Crespo, Ramon wrote:
> Hello All,
> Over the weekend the machine randomly rebooted over the weekend if there any
> logs or anything I should be looking at to find out why someone please let
> me know. Ive had uptimes of 3 weeks on it and then it randomly reboots. Note
> its a DEC Alpha PWS 600au with 256MB of ram and its currently running
> 4.3-RELEASE.

Alpha machines don't clear the dmesg buffer during reboot.
So if it was a panic you can read the panic message after reboot
using dmesg.
If you don't see older boot messages it usually means a power loss.

